  "parent": {
    "approval_scope": "The workspace declared in `docs/ui/design-manifest.yaml`. Campaign Portfolio (portfolio and campaign detail), Retail health, and Prompt Administration carry the command-center visual language. From revision `2026-10-08.1`, the Scorecard, Reach and funnel, Audiences, Retention, and Repeat purchase by product packages, and from revision `2026-10-09.1` the New customers package, carry the information-architecture visual language; each is implemented only in its own build slice, once that slice's prerequisites and route approval are met. The channel, product, marketplace, evidence-health, and media-efficiency pages are retired from the frontend; their presentation APIs remain deployed for reuse",
    "implementation_decision_date": "2026-10-07",
    "implementation_disposition": "approved_for_implementation",
    "path": "docs/ui/README.md",
    "sha256": "1d4e65da4ab910b1db34a4e717f56d9952c0598d443100c2b89a9f7019440341",
    "status": "Approved for implementation — manifest revision `2026-10-09.2` (revised 2026-10-09 — business outcomes wave 2b revises four page packages: New customers adds new buyers and cost per new buyer per channel under the platform tiles, with `NewCustomersArtifact` v2; Audiences labels each segment by its provider, Amazon or third party, and states that DSP behaviour segments and Amazon audience segments use different IDs and are never linked; Retention adds the designed state for a vintage built on calendar-quarter cohorts, and its scope band names the cohort grain; Reach and funnel relabels the funnel's branded-search rate as search rate, because AMC's documentation doesn't say searchConversion is a branded search; approved under the owner's UI/IA approval of 2026-10-07 (owner-decisions-ui.md) with owner ratification of the revision pending; the Scorecard's open item for New customers names the v2 artifact, with no change to the Scorecard's design; every other package is carried forward unchanged. Prior revision `2026-10-09.1` (2026-10-09) — adds the New customers page package, built from the information-architecture New customers mockup and the business outcomes design, approved under the owner's UI/IA approval of 2026-10-07 (owner-decisions-ui.md) with owner ratification of the package pending; the Scorecard's open item for New customers now points to that package, with no change to the Scorecard's design; every other package is carried forward unchanged. Prior revision `2026-10-08.1` (2026-10-08) — adds the Scorecard, Reach and funnel, Audiences, Retention and Repeat purchase by product page packages, built from the UI and information-architecture mockups and design, and one Retail health page action that links to Repeat purchase by product, with no change to its time model; approved under the owner's UI/IA approval of 2026-10-07 (owner-decisions-ui.md); the campaign-portfolio and prompt-administration packages are carried forward unchanged. Prior revision `2026-10-01.1` (2026-10-01) — monetary values display at two decimal places from a server-derived display value on the campaign portfolio, campaign detail, retail health, and the metric-focus dialog, which moves to `MetricFocus.v3` (ADR-084), and prompt versions state who created them, by email resolved at read time (ADR-069 amendment); the campaign-portfolio mockup is carried forward unchanged. Prior revision `2026-09-25.1` (2026-09-25) — the insight and metric-focus dialogs rebalance — the deep analysis renders as a full-width band beneath the dialog's evidence with readings three-up wide, the insight dialog goes single-column, provenance collapses to one customer-word strip, and no citations or internal vocabulary render anywhere customer-facing — grounding verification stays server-side. Prior revision `2026-09-24.1` (2026-09-24) — the campaign detail summary metrics render as a uniform two-row × four-column grid of equal tiles, superseding the labeled section grouping and, for that strip only, the single-row card-group rule; also carries the ADR-076 slice D prompt-administration wire-contract amendment, tier dimension and fragment digests. Prior revision `2026-09-23.4` carried insight absence states per the [insight-presentation contract](insight-presentation-contract.md) and the 2026-09-23 UX revisions — single-row equal-height card groups, raised type-tier contrast with full-strength card body text, full-width retail insight rows, 10-row display paging, and the in-detail campaign switcher; accepted 2026-09-23; frontend implementation delivered and live-verified 2026-09-24)"
  },
